\section{3+1 Decomposition and Evolution Equations}

The spacetime manifold is decomposed using the ADM 3+1 formalism:
\begin{equation}
ds^2 = -\alpha^2 dt^2 + \gamma_{ij}
(dx^i + \beta^i dt)(dx^j + \beta^j dt),
\label{eq:adm}
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\alpha$ is the lapse,
    \item $\beta^i$ is the shift vector,
    \item $\gamma_{ij}$ is the spatial metric.
\end{itemize}

The evolution equations are:
\begin{align}
\partial_t \gamma_{ij}
&= -2\alpha K_{ij}
+ \mathcal{L}_{\beta} \gamma_{ij},
\label{eq:gamma_evolve}
\\[6pt]
\partial_t K_{ij}
&= -\nabla_i \nabla_j \alpha
+ \alpha (R_{ij} - 2K_{ik}K^k{}_j + K K_{ij})
+ \mathcal{L}_{\beta} K_{ij}
- 8\pi\alpha S_{ij}.
\label{eq:K_evolve}
\end{align}

These equations govern all manifold evolution modules.

