\section{Constraint Solvers}

The Hamiltonian constraint:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}
= R + K^2 - K_{ij}K^{ij}
- 16\pi \rho = 0,
\label{eq:hamiltonian}
\end{equation}

The momentum constraint:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{M}^i
= \nabla_j (K^{ij} - \gamma^{ij}K)
- 8\pi S^i = 0.
\label{eq:momentum}
\end{equation}

Constraint damping uses:
\begin{equation}
\partial_t \mathcal{H}
= -\kappa_H \mathcal{H},
\qquad
\partial_t \mathcal{M}^i
= -\kappa_M \mathcal{M}^i,
\label{eq:damping}
\end{equation}
with $\kappa_H, \kappa_M > 0$ tuned for manifold stability.

