\section{Finite-Difference Discretization}

Spatial derivatives use 4th-order centered finite differences:
\begin{equation}
\partial_x f_i
= \frac{-f_{i+2} + 8f_{i+1} - 8f_{i-1} + f_{i-2}}{12\Delta x}.
\label{eq:fd4}
\end{equation}

Time evolution uses 4th-order Runge--Kutta:
\begin{equation}
f^{n+1}
= f^n + \frac{1}{6}(k_1 + 2k_2 + 2k_3 + k_4).
\label{eq:rk4}
\end{equation}

CFL stability condition:
\begin{equation}
\Delta t
\leq 0.25 \frac{\Delta x}{c}.
\label{eq:cfl}
\end{equation}

