\section{Adaptive Mesh Refinement (AMR)}

AMR refinement triggers on curvature invariants:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{I}
= R_{\mu\nu\rho\sigma}R^{\mu\nu\rho\sigma},
\label{eq:kretschmann}
\end{equation}
and quantum pressure gradients:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{Q}
= \left| \nabla_\mu \langle T^{\mu\nu} \rangle \right|.
\label{eq:qgradient}
\end{equation}

Refinement condition:
\begin{equation}
\text{Refine if }
\mathcal{I} > \mathcal{I}_{\text{crit}}
\quad \text{or} \quad
\mathcal{Q} > \mathcal{Q}_{\text{crit}}.
\label{eq:refine}
\end{equation}

Coarsening condition:
\begin{equation}
\text{Coarsen if }
\mathcal{I} < 0.1\,\mathcal{I}_{\text{crit}}
\quad \text{and} \quad
\mathcal{Q} < 0.1\,\mathcal{Q}_{\text{crit}}.
\label{eq:coarsen}
\end{equation}

