where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\Delta \mathbf{z}(t)$ is deviation from target manifold,
    \item $K$ is the gain matrix,
    \item $\Phi_{\sigma}$ is the nonlinear correction term,
    \item $\sigma \in \{+1,-1\}$ selects manifold mode.
\end{itemize}

This solver governs wormhole, Kerr--Newman, white-hole, hydro, and
atmospheric modules under a single autonomous architecture.

